Restrict package loading to the current module.

When no include prefixes are given, gta loads the "..." pattern, which in
module-aware mode means every package of every module in the build list --
including packages of dependencies that the main module never imports. Those
packages have imports of their own that a tidied go.mod does not record, so the
go command aborts the whole load with:

    go: updates to go.mod needed; to update it:
        go mod tidy

"./..." keeps the reverse dependency graph scoped to the packages gta can
actually report on, which is all a per-repository change detector needs.

--- a/packager.go
+++ b/packager.go
@@ -273,7 +273,7 @@
 	}
 
 	if loadAllPackages {
-		patterns = []string{"..."}
+		patterns = []string{"./..."}
 	}
 
 	loadedPackages, err := packages.Load(cfg, patterns...)
